/* ------------------------------------------- Canvas: BO follows the shell continuum, the Main panel keeps its flat one
   Two rules used to sit here painting an opaque #FFF1DC (dark #2C2E38) over BOTH html and body on
   every bo-charcoal page with !important. bo-charcoal-shell.css declares the locked light and dark
   canvas continuum (DESIGN.md -> Light mode surfaces: "Continuum ... Canvas only;
   background-attachment: fixed") on html and keeps body transparent, but that rule carries no
   !important, so the flatten always won the cascade: ~108 pages painted one flat cream while the
   Member / Transaction families (11 bo-wallet-tx pages) and two pages rescued by bo-page-canvas.css (that sheet
   has since been deleted - its three rules were a per-page copy of this same continuum) showed the continuum - one
   shell, two canvases, differing on a page switch.
   Owner decision 2026-09-30 ("所有的bo 网页背景"): BO follows the continuum. The Main panel is a
   separate portal with its own shell (AGENTS.md: do not unify the Main panel), so it keeps the flat
   canvas it always had - owner chose "只 BO，Main panel 恢复纯色".

   The Main panel's pages are recognised by the classes its own shell gives them, each verified to
   appear on NO bo-charcoal BO page: main-mod-page, provider-exec, accounting-settlement-page,
   main-provider-create-page, main-provider-integration-page, main-report-exec-page, main-report-page.
   main-admin-detail-page and main-admin-create-page could NOT be used for this: they also sit on
   admin-user-create / role-create / game-provider-create, which are BO pages. main-profile and
   main-stat-detail carry no distinguishing class at all (their body is exactly the BO shell), so
   they opt out explicitly with bo-flat-canvas - a page that needs the flat canvas says so itself.
   The same applies to the agent portal (12 agent-modern pages, plus agent-login / login which carry
   bo-login-body) and to every Main page above: none of these classes sits on a BO shell page, so
   outside the BO shell nothing changes canvas at all - measured, not assumed from an opaque wrapper.
   The Main REPORT family needs no entry here: main-report-charcoal.css already declares the same
   continuum for it against [data-access-page], so those pages were never meant to be flat.
   Inner surfaces that legitimately sit on #FFF1DC (control wells, zebra rows, chips, permission
   groups) keep their own rules and are untouched. */
html:not([data-bo-theme="dark"]) body.report-body.bo-charcoal:is(.main-mod-page,.provider-exec,.accounting-settlement-page,.main-provider-create-page,.main-provider-integration-page,.main-report-exec-page,.main-report-page,.agent-modern,.bo-login-body,.bo-flat-canvas),
html:not([data-bo-theme="dark"]):has(body.report-body.bo-charcoal:is(.main-mod-page,.provider-exec,.accounting-settlement-page,.main-provider-create-page,.main-provider-integration-page,.main-report-exec-page,.main-report-page,.agent-modern,.bo-login-body,.bo-flat-canvas)){
